 "final_summary": "The bug was in the sorting logic where a leading '-' in the sort parameter (like '-priority') was incorrectly interpreted as ascending instead of descending. The fix modified the `parse_sort` function in `tracker/query.py` to set the direction to 'DESC' when a leading '-' is detected, and properly removes the '-' from the field name. This ensures that sort parameters with a leading '-' correctly produce descending order.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/query.py b/tracker/query.py\nindex 3166a82..fc95899 100644\n--- a/tracker/query.py\n+++ b/tracker/query.py\n@@ -19,10 +19,9 @@ def parse_sort(value):\n         part = raw.strip()\n         if not part:\n             continue\n-        direction = \"ASC\"\n-        if part.startswith(\"-\"):\n-            direction = \"ASC\"\n-            part = part[1:]\n+        if part.startswith(\"-\"): \n+            direction = \"DESC\"\n+            part = part[1:] \n         if part not in SORTABLE_FIELDS:\n             raise ValidationError(f\"cannot sort by {part}\", {\"sort\": \"invalid\"})\n         order.append((part, direction))\n",
 "evaluation": {
